values ('f3a4b5c6-8d9e-4f63-8a23-3b4c5d6e7f33', 'diversity-oppression-and-social-justice', 'Diversity, Oppression, and Social Justice', 'This course examines diversity, power, privilege, oppression, resistance, and liberation as central concerns of generalist social work. Using intersectional, anti-racist, anti-oppressive, decolonizing, disability-justice, feminist, queer, human-rights, and environmental-justice lenses, students analyze how identities and social locations are shaped by institutions, histories, policies, and everyday relationships. Through critical reflection, case analysis, dialogue, community knowledge, and applied advocacy, students build the humility and practical skill to engage difference, challenge injustice, share power, and pursue accountable change with individuals, families, groups, organizations, and communities.');

